{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2189-02-13 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. ___. I'm Dr. ___, one of your hospitalists. You're here today for your scheduled chemotherapy with methotrexate, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2189-02-13 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. I’ve been doing well at home. No fevers, no nausea, nothing unusual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2189-02-13 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. We’ll be giving you high-dose methotrexate today, along with sodium bicarbonate to protect your kidneys and leucovorin later to help clear the drug safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2189-02-13 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from last time. The bicarbonate drip, right? It makes me feel a bit jittery sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2189-02-13 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, some patients feel that way. We’ll monitor you closely and adjust the rate if needed. Your labs this morning look stable—creatinine is 1.0, which is good for your kidney function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2189-02-13 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my sodium? I know it’s been a little low before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2189-02-13 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was 133 today, which is slightly low but not concerning yet. We’ll keep an eye on it, especially since you’re on desmopressin for diabetes insipidus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2189-02-13 11:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I take it twice a day like prescribed. I just hate getting up so much at night to pee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2189-02-13 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But taking extra sprays can lower your sodium too much, which can be dangerous—could even lead to seizures. We’ll talk more about that later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2189-02-13 11:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be careful. I just want to get through this chemo and go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2189-02-13 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve started the methotrexate through your port. It’ll run over a few hours. Nursing will check your vitals regularly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2189-02-13 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. Any side effects I should watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2189-02-13 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most people feel okay during the infusion. Later, you might feel a bit nauseous, but we’ve got ondansetron if needed. Mouth sores can happen too, so we’ll start rinsing with baking soda solution."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2189-02-13 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Methotrexate is nearly done. We’re increasing your bicarbonate drip to 175 cc/hr to help flush it out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2189-02-13 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. My mouth feels a little dry, but that’s it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2189-02-13 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common. Drink small sips of water and keep using the mouth rinse. We’ll check your methotrexate level tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2189-02-14 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your methotrexate level last night was 4.2, which is expected. We’ll keep the bicarbonate going and start leucovorin to help clear it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2189-02-14 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that a good number?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2189-02-14 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s exactly what we expect after the first day. It needs to drop below 0.1 before we feel fully comfortable, so we’ll check again tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2189-02-14 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. My back’s been a little achy—could that be from the meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2189-02-14 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We can give you acetaminophen if needed. But we’ll make sure it’s not a kidney issue—your urine output looks good so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2189-02-14 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re increasing your bicarbonate to 200 cc/hr. Your labs are stable, and your blood pressure is good—128 over 76."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2189-02-14 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You said my lisinopril was held. Should I be worried about my blood pressure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2189-02-14 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it’s standard to hold it during chemo to protect your kidneys. We’ll restart it before you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2189-02-14 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. I take it every morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2189-02-15 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your methotrexate level dropped to 0.27 last night. That’s a great sign. We’ll check one more time tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2189-02-15 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s going down fast. Does that mean I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2189-02-15 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly tomorrow, if the next level is low enough. But we also need to talk about your sodium."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2189-02-15 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2189-02-15 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s dropping—now 126. We think it’s because you might be using more desmopressin than prescribed to avoid frequent urination."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2189-02-15 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I admit I sometimes take an extra spray at night. I just want to sleep through the night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2189-02-15 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand, but low sodium can cause confusion, seizures, or even be life-threatening. We’d like to give you a dose of Lasix tomorrow to help balance it and recheck the level before discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2189-02-15 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to stay another day. I feel fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2189-02-15 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I hear you. But we need to make sure you’re safe. We’ll give Lasix in the morning and check your sodium. If it’s improving, you can go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2189-02-15 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, but I really need to get home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your methotrexate level is now 0.10—excellent. But your sodium is 124, which is quite low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s bad, isn’t it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’re giving you 20 mg of IV Lasix and stopping your fluids. We strongly recommend staying to recheck your sodium."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I understand, but I need to go home today. I’ll be careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You need to understand the risks—seizures, confusion, even death from very low sodium. We’re documenting that you’re leaving against medical advice on this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hear you. I’ll get my labs checked tomorrow like you said. I promise."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We’ll restart your lisinopril and send you home with instructions. Please call us with your lab results."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. And I’ll cut back on the desmopressin—I promise."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Continue your temozolomide as scheduled—7 days on, 7 days off. And keep taking your lamotrigine for seizures."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t had a seizure in a long time. Brain MRI was stable last time, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your lymphoma is in remission. That’s why we’re continuing the maintenance plan every four months."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m grateful for that. It’s been a long road."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Just one more thing—keep taking Flomax for your kidney stones, and avoid dehydration."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll see you in four months for your next cycle. Please follow up with Dr. ___ too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make the appointment today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. And call us if you feel dizzy, confused, or unwell before your labs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. ___. We’re glad you tolerated chemo well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Me too. See you in a few months."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll be here. Drive safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. My son’s picking me up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Let him know about the sodium issue too, just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll tell him everything. Thanks for looking out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s what we’re here for. Rest well and stay hydrated—but not too much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Not too much water, and no extra desmopressin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:56:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. You’ve got the plan down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:57:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll follow it to the letter."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:58:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’ll talk soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2189-02-16 06:59:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Take care, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2189-02-16 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2189-02-16 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "See you next time."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2189-02-13 10:40:00",
    "admission_end": "2189-02-16 14:37:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 65-year-old man with a history of primary CNS diffuse large B-cell lymphoma in remission was admitted for scheduled maintenance chemotherapy with high-dose methotrexate. He tolerated the infusion well without significant side effects. Methotrexate levels declined appropriately, reaching 0.10 by the morning of discharge, indicating effective clearance. His renal function remained stable throughout. However, hyponatremia worsened to 124 mEq/L, likely due to overuse of desmopressin for diabetes insipidus, which the patient admitted to using extra doses to reduce nocturia. Despite medical advice to remain for sodium recheck after Lasix administration, the patient declined and chose to be discharged home. Lisinopril was restarted for hypertension, and he was instructed to follow up on labs and continue temozolomide and seizure prophylaxis. The plan includes return in four months for the next chemotherapy cycle.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Diffuse large B-cell lymphoma, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Diabetes insipidus",
      "Hypo-osmolality and hyponatremia",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Calculus of kidney",
      "Insomnia, unspecified",
      "Personal history of nicotine dependence",
      "Presence of artificial hip joint, bilateral"
    ]
  }
}
